WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.973
A T-shirt printer pays rent for its workshop, and buys a blank shirt for every T-shirt it prints.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:16.864
Rent is five hundred dollars at any output. Blank shirts cost four dollars each. Add them for total cost. Even at zero output, the rent must be paid.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.752
So total cost rises as output rises, but never falls below the fixed cost.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:37.875
Steps one and two. Work out total variable cost: cost per unit times units. Then add the fixed cost. For one hundred and fifty shirts: six hundred dollars plus five hundred is one thousand one hundred dollars.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:45.203
If total cost is given, subtract instead. Fixed cost is total cost minus variable cost.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:53.717
Steps three and four. Write it in one line, fixed cost plus cost per unit times quantity, and give the answer with currency.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:12.120
Here is a real question from November 2021. A firm has fixed costs of fifty thousand dollars a month and variable costs of two hundred and fifty dollars per unit. It makes seven hundred and fifty units a month. Calculate total costs per month. Two marks.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:17.181
Pick out the three figures: the fixed cost, the cost per unit, and the output.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:26.912
Total variable cost is two hundred and fifty times seven hundred and fifty, which is one hundred and eighty-seven thousand five hundred dollars.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:41.859
Add the fixed cost. Fifty thousand plus one hundred and eighty-seven thousand five hundred is two hundred and thirty-seven thousand five hundred dollars. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:46.301
The variable part is much bigger here. Together they make the total.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:53.264
A common mistake is adding the cost per unit to the fixed cost without multiplying by output.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:59.835
Another is dividing by output. That gives average cost, but the question asks for the total.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:15.701
Now you try. A food van has fixed costs of one thousand two hundred dollars a month. Ingredients cost two dollars fifty per meal, and it sells nine hundred meals a month. Calculate total costs per month. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:29.405
Variable cost is two dollars fifty times nine hundred, which is two thousand two hundred and fifty dollars. Add one thousand two hundred: total cost is three thousand four hundred and fifty dollars.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:35.549
Check the picture: a small fixed cost and a larger variable cost add up to the total.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:44.291
Remember: cost per unit times quantity, add the fixed cost, and give the total with currency. Now try the practice questions.
